A||||9||Pheagey||junk yard rim question||||1||
Z||000000||Pheagey||11-17-2001||10:43 PM||||   I'll be goin to a salavge yard Monday evening to pick out some rims and tires to last me a few months till I can buy some new tires (mine were stolen, rims and all.).<BR>   mny question is whats the rim specs for the fiero? I'f I come across a nice set of 15-16" rims I'll get them instead of the stock pontiac sport rims that came w/ it. I dunno if it helps but I got an '88 coupe.<BR>thanks.<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000001||watts||11-17-2001||10:48 PM||||You can get away with anything (almost) that's a 5*100mm pattern.  The offset may or may not be right...  but it's only temporary right?<P>Asthetics are at your discretion.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MR2KLR||11-17-2001||10:48 PM||||Here is what I know, They are a 5 lug X 100mm ppl. say that 45mm offset is good for the 88's hope I helped some<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOYPICS/scrapbookFiles/importD3.gif"> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A> <A HREF="mailto:Tomtom81@webtv.net">Tomtom81@webtv.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||12:43 AM||||any 14", 15",or 16" Grand Am, Beretta or similar mid sized GM FWD rim will fit. Also Dodge Neon, Shadow, and FWD Celica will work too. I would look for the 15 or 16 inch Grand Am wheels. If you can find nice ones in the bone yard, they look pretty good on the Fiero and say Pontiac on them. I swiped the wheels and tires from my wife's 96 Grand Am for a show and they were pretty impressive. I didn't win anything though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pheagey||11-18-2001||02:16 PM||||Kool thanks guys, thats some really helpful info 'bout the rims. Now what about the rubber, whats the deal with the numbers? I know there like 205/60/15. the 15 is the rim size right? whats the other two?<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed.<BR>"The car formerly know as Dj's Fiero."||||reg||1
Z||000005||watts||11-18-2001||02:42 PM||||Ok, let's take a 205/60-15 as an example.<P>205 - width of the tread in mm's (divide by 25.4 for inches)<P>60 - aspect ratio.  In this case, the height of the rubber from the rim to the tread surface is 60% of the width (205 in this case), so 123mm high.<P>15 - rim diameter in inches.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pheagey||11-19-2001||07:11 AM||||so what would the numbers be for rubber that fits onto a 16" rim? 205/40/16?<BR>*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000007||WampusCat||11-19-2001||08:18 AM||||205/60/15  like mentioned above, 205mm X .60 = 123mm sidewall.<BR>205/40/16 205mm X .40 = 82mm sidewall + extra 1/2"(12.7mm) from bigger wheel = 94.7mm so would be smaller diameter tire than 205/60/15.  205/55/16 would be closest. <A HREF="http://www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html" TARGET=_blank>www.miata.net/garage/tirecalc.html</A>  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pheagey||11-19-2001||10:15 AM||||Hey thanks for that link.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">MMMmmm wheels...&lt;drooling&gt;||||reg||10
Z||000009||GodSend||11-19-2001||11:35 AM||||As a general guideline, anything lower then a 55 sidewall is considered "low profile" or sport.. Of course this does depend a little on the other 2 numbers,...||||reg||1
